cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this benchmark, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "live-events-llm-benchmarks: A Code-Scored Benchmark for Natural-Language Live-Event Search"
version: 0.1.0
date-released: 2026-10-27
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.23681408
authors:
  - family-names: Kalyanasundaram
    given-names: Balajee
    affiliation: Independent Researcher
    email: balajeekalyanasundaram@ieee.org
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0007-7292-2417"
repository-code: "https://github.com/balajeekalyan/live-events-llm-benchmarks"
license: MIT
abstract: >-
  A benchmark for natural-language live-event search with tool-calling LLM
  agents: a seeded synthetic catalog of 1,200 events and 5,669 dated
  occurrences, 400 queries labeled with machine-readable constraints in nine
  slices, and a scorer that computes gold answers from the constraints with the
  same matching code the search tool uses, so no LLM judge is needed. Includes
  single-prompt, routed, content-control and type-neutral systems built on
  figureout.
keywords:
  - large language models
  - tool calling
  - agent routing
  - benchmark
  - function calling
  - consumer assistants
